WEBVTT

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:08.440
Dealing with Sakurai can really drain a guy.

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:18.950
We got off with just being detained to our homes this time, but who knows about the next.

00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:27.000
But you guys saved those of us riding the KiHa 52 from crashing, remember?

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:28.460
That's definitely a silver lining.

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:33.840
Still, you had to miss the trip.

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:35.180
Yeah.

00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:37.470
I was pretty bummed, you know.

00:00:44.230 --> 00:00:45.600
That was close.

00:00:46.150 --> 00:00:50.480
Safety first, now, Mr. Driver.

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:51.990
I'm sorry.

00:00:52.610 --> 00:00:55.110
I swear I'll pay you back for the trip fees.

00:00:55.490 --> 00:00:58.990
As long as you're safe, Takayama, it's all good.

00:00:58.990 --> 00:00:59.990
Bye!

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:14.380
What's this?

00:03:21.510 --> 00:03:26.850
The energy necessary for running is made by burning fat and glycogen.

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:33.650
In times when endurance is required,
energy is mostly burned from fat.

00:03:34.360 --> 00:03:35.400
This is perfect.

00:03:36.070 --> 00:03:38.320
At least, it should be.

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:41.280
If I don't change, I'll just be a burden.

00:03:41.610 --> 00:03:43.780
I've gotta try a little harder!

00:03:45.490 --> 00:03:47.030
M-Ms. Iida?

00:03:47.910 --> 00:03:52.080
I-I'm sorry, I really should be at home.

00:03:52.920 --> 00:03:56.920
You do realize I'm under the same orders, right?

00:03:56.920 --> 00:03:58.800
We just have to not get caught!

00:03:59.170 --> 00:04:00.880
You've really been working out there.

00:04:01.510 --> 00:04:05.180
I, um, wanted to be more usefulвЂ”

00:04:05.720 --> 00:04:07.050
To Takayama?

00:04:08.930 --> 00:04:11.680
T-To everyone in K4!

00:04:16.110 --> 00:04:18.360
Sakurai's not picking up.

00:04:21.030 --> 00:04:22.610
Hey, Koumi?

00:04:22.610 --> 00:04:24.910
It's Takayama. Can you talk?

00:04:24.910 --> 00:04:26.870
Yeah, I can.

00:04:27.530 --> 00:04:28.450
Yeah.

00:04:29.160 --> 00:04:29.870
Yeah.

00:04:30.330 --> 00:04:31.330
Huh?

00:04:31.330 --> 00:04:36.000
The Yamanote Line is now arriving.

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:37.380
A missed call?

00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:40.250
What's Takayama want?
He knows I can't answer in the train.

00:04:41.670 --> 00:04:44.010
Maybe I should call him back.

00:04:48.550 --> 00:04:49.890
Haruka?

00:04:56.270 --> 00:04:57.270
Koumi!

00:04:58.310 --> 00:04:59.690
Takayama!

00:04:59.690 --> 00:05:01.980
Sorry for calling you out of the blue.

00:05:01.980 --> 00:05:04.490
Oh, it's fine.

00:05:05.740 --> 00:05:08.160
Someone might spot us. Let's change areas.

00:05:09.370 --> 00:05:11.740
So, what did you want to talk about?

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:18.380
What?

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:20.420
I thought it was a prank at first.

00:05:20.420 --> 00:05:22.550
But if it's true...

00:05:23.210 --> 00:05:26.590
Like, that bomber on the Ashio Line could have had an accomplice!

00:05:26.590 --> 00:05:28.180
There's no wayвЂ”

00:05:28.180 --> 00:05:30.970
Hiya! I'm Tsubarail and I love JNR!

00:05:30.970 --> 00:05:35.770
Do you rail kids wanna take the 25,000 km challenge?!

00:05:39.190 --> 00:05:41.650
Let's find somewhere quieter.

00:05:43.480 --> 00:05:44.860
Railsies.

00:06:02.210 --> 00:06:05.920
Grandfather, where are we going?

00:06:12.220 --> 00:06:13.850
We should be good here.

00:06:15.560 --> 00:06:17.140
So, back on topic.

00:06:18.100 --> 00:06:23.730
Assuming the Ashio Line guy did have an accomplice, if he's after me...

00:06:23.730 --> 00:06:26.190
Oh! Aoi could be in trouble!

00:06:26.190 --> 00:06:27.740
I'll call her.

00:06:30.910 --> 00:06:35.120
Good timing. I was just about to call you.

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:36.000
Right now, I'mвЂ”

00:06:42.040 --> 00:06:43.340
Hello?

00:06:43.340 --> 00:06:44.210
Aoi?

00:06:44.210 --> 00:06:46.010
Hey, what happened?

00:06:46.010 --> 00:06:47.630
Koumi, how's Sakurai?

00:06:54.140 --> 00:06:55.310
This way.

00:06:55.310 --> 00:06:57.100
H-Hey, Koumi!

00:06:58.930 --> 00:07:00.850
We have to tread lightly.

00:07:00.850 --> 00:07:02.810
Someone's after your life, Takayama.

00:07:05.230 --> 00:07:08.820
This is actually making me miss Iwaizumi.

00:07:08.820 --> 00:07:10.660
I got this!

00:07:11.610 --> 00:07:15.330
He burst onto the curry-eating championship scene and is all anyone can talk about!

00:07:15.330 --> 00:07:19.000
He cleaned 20 plates in 10 minutes during the preliminaries!

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:22.040
Does he understand what
"confined to our homes" means?

00:07:23.460 --> 00:07:25.710
My poor phone broke.

00:07:26.920 --> 00:07:28.090
Haruka...

00:07:28.090 --> 00:07:29.420
and Takayama?

00:07:30.340 --> 00:07:32.390
What are they doing?

00:07:34.970 --> 00:07:37.600
Do they understand what
"confined to our homes" means?

00:07:37.600 --> 00:07:42.100
Takayama's kind-hearted, not spineless.

00:07:42.350 --> 00:07:44.770
He's not just spineless.

00:07:44.770 --> 00:07:46.360
He's using it to get her in the sack!

00:07:46.730 --> 00:07:50.070
Good thing I got my gun back,
so I can put a bullet in his brain.

00:07:53.450 --> 00:07:54.370
A sniper!

00:07:54.370 --> 00:07:55.660
R-Really?

00:07:57.240 --> 00:07:58.910
We have to run!

00:07:58.910 --> 00:07:59.540
Right!

00:07:59.540 --> 00:08:00.450
Huh?

00:08:00.450 --> 00:08:01.040
Hey!

00:08:01.040 --> 00:08:02.120
Crap!

00:08:02.120 --> 00:08:04.710
Hiya! I'm Tsubarail and I love JNR!

00:08:04.710 --> 00:08:06.420
Do you rail kids wannaвЂ”

00:08:06.420 --> 00:08:08.300
Shut up! You made me shoot at them!

00:08:08.300 --> 00:08:09.880
Railsies.
And why're those two getting the wrong idea?

00:08:09.880 --> 00:08:10.630
And why're those two getting the wrong idea?

00:08:14.800 --> 00:08:16.970
You, girl! Stop!

00:08:23.810 --> 00:08:25.350
What do you want?

00:08:26.860 --> 00:08:28.440
Stop!

00:08:28.940 --> 00:08:31.860
Someone's chasing us, Koumi!

00:08:31.860 --> 00:08:35.070
Don't look back! Just focus on running away!

00:08:35.070 --> 00:08:37.950
If you don't stop, I have permission to use force!

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:39.620
Why is this happening?

00:08:39.620 --> 00:08:40.700
Hey!

00:08:43.290 --> 00:08:45.040
Someone up above must hate me.

00:08:59.760 --> 00:09:02.520
Takayama, are you hurt?

00:09:03.230 --> 00:09:05.140
What about you?

00:09:05.560 --> 00:09:08.230
Looks like we aren't being chased anymore.

00:09:08.230 --> 00:09:09.860
I guess we lost them.

00:09:12.940 --> 00:09:13.780
What's wrong?

00:09:13.780 --> 00:09:16.280
Oh, nothing.

00:09:16.280 --> 00:09:19.030
More importantly, we should contact Ms. Iida.

00:09:19.030 --> 00:09:21.040
She might be able to help.

00:09:21.040 --> 00:09:23.540
Oh, Ms. Iida! Good idea!

00:09:23.540 --> 00:09:28.670
The phone you are trying to reach is either out of service range or turned off.

00:09:28.670 --> 00:09:29.790
No dice.

00:09:29.790 --> 00:09:30.380
The phone you are trying to reach is either out of service range or turned off.

00:09:32.760 --> 00:09:34.840
H-How did they find us?

00:09:36.010 --> 00:09:36.970
Th-Through your phone!

00:09:36.970 --> 00:09:40.760
They must have triangulated
your location via that cellphone!

00:09:40.760 --> 00:09:41.810
Get rid of it!

00:09:41.810 --> 00:09:42.970
O-Okay!

00:09:51.150 --> 00:09:54.280
Yay, power!

00:09:54.280 --> 00:09:58.360
You're slipping. What if there was an emergency?

00:09:58.360 --> 00:10:00.280
Well, I'm confined to my house.

00:10:00.620 --> 00:10:04.790
Besides, it's common sense that you can
charge your phone with alkaline batteries.

00:10:04.790 --> 00:10:07.790
Thanks for teaching me then, Hitomi.

00:10:08.170 --> 00:10:11.170
You're paying for my coffee.

00:10:20.470 --> 00:10:21.390
I'm sorry.

00:10:21.850 --> 00:10:23.100
This is my fault.

00:10:24.310 --> 00:10:25.980
Don't worry about it.

00:10:25.980 --> 00:10:26.810
Here.

00:10:28.020 --> 00:10:29.520
Thanks.

00:10:35.110 --> 00:10:38.740
You know, being able to help you makes me...

00:10:39.530 --> 00:10:40.870
pretty happy.

00:10:40.870 --> 00:10:41.620
Huh?

00:10:56.300 --> 00:10:57.420
What's going on?

00:10:58.010 --> 00:10:59.680
Why are cats chasing us?

00:11:04.180 --> 00:11:05.100
Takayama!

00:11:08.770 --> 00:11:13.690
I've read in books that people can train dogs as assassins.

00:11:13.690 --> 00:11:16.530
Maybe that's what these cats are!

00:11:16.530 --> 00:11:18.490
Th-That's impossible!

00:11:19.900 --> 00:11:23.320
Are they really following us?

00:11:24.070 --> 00:11:25.280
It's our smell.

00:11:25.280 --> 00:11:27.750
Like police dogs, they're tracking us by smell!

00:11:27.750 --> 00:11:29.660
Your smell?

00:11:36.090 --> 00:11:37.300
No way.

00:11:37.960 --> 00:11:40.380
We have to get away!

00:11:43.840 --> 00:11:47.180
Guess I managed to lose that police officer.

00:11:47.810 --> 00:11:48.970
Hup!

00:11:52.560 --> 00:11:54.650
Look at this mess.

00:12:06.030 --> 00:12:07.410
That building.

00:12:10.540 --> 00:12:12.540
Is this Haruka's?

00:12:16.670 --> 00:12:17.750
Koumi!

00:12:21.670 --> 00:12:25.840
What do we do? You can't go around looking like that.

00:12:25.840 --> 00:12:27.930
It's okay. I don't mind.

00:12:31.060 --> 00:12:33.190
We've gotta find a place to hide!

00:12:33.190 --> 00:12:34.690
R-Right!

00:12:43.610 --> 00:12:48.030
Should we really be sneaking in here?

00:12:48.030 --> 00:12:51.790
Maybe they'll forgive us when we explain it's life-or-death.

00:12:55.580 --> 00:12:57.580
The Transportation Museum.

00:12:58.290 --> 00:13:00.170
You've been here before, Koumi?

00:13:02.510 --> 00:13:03.300
Yeah.

00:13:05.050 --> 00:13:08.010
Koumi, it looks like we can get in through here.

00:13:10.470 --> 00:13:11.140
Koumi?

00:13:13.140 --> 00:13:13.850
Again?

00:13:13.850 --> 00:13:15.060
Don't look at me!

00:13:15.060 --> 00:13:15.600
Huh?

00:13:15.600 --> 00:13:17.600
Turn around for a second.

00:13:17.600 --> 00:13:19.020
O-Okay.

00:13:20.730 --> 00:13:22.480
Suck it up, Haruka.

00:13:22.780 --> 00:13:25.860
This is to keep Takayama alive.

00:13:31.040 --> 00:13:32.410
Now, while they're distracted!

00:13:41.170 --> 00:13:46.720
Weird that the door was just conveniently open.

00:13:51.140 --> 00:13:53.220
Something's not right.

00:13:53.220 --> 00:13:54.310
Yeah.

00:13:54.310 --> 00:13:59.100
Maybe the attacking cats
were only part of a larger trap.

00:13:59.100 --> 00:14:04.280
Their real objective was to
corner you in this building.

00:14:04.280 --> 00:14:07.320
Koumi, you're overthinking this.

00:14:18.370 --> 00:14:22.250
Takayama, you can't turn back the clock.

00:14:22.710 --> 00:14:25.670
If something happened to you, I...

00:14:26.880 --> 00:14:28.050
Koumi.

00:14:38.850 --> 00:14:40.310
I remember this place.

00:14:41.650 --> 00:14:43.400
Kodama Restaurant.

00:14:44.230 --> 00:14:47.570
On the fourth floor of the Transportation Museum.

00:14:47.570 --> 00:14:48.650
Have you ever been there?

00:14:49.780 --> 00:14:53.330
It's an eatery that revives the interior of the dining cars

00:14:53.330 --> 00:14:57.580
on the 151 series Kodama Express,
the car that built the grand beginnings of JNR.

00:15:02.210 --> 00:15:04.800
Not that its menu was impressive or anything.

00:15:05.590 --> 00:15:10.090
But I could never wait to eat there when I dragged my parents to the museum.

00:15:20.890 --> 00:15:22.020
Sakurai!

00:15:23.020 --> 00:15:27.990
You've got some guts, walking around when you were ordered to stay home.

00:15:27.990 --> 00:15:29.700
Yeah, really.

00:15:29.700 --> 00:15:32.950
Oh, uh, you see...

00:15:33.370 --> 00:15:36.950
You see what happens when you don't set
a good example for your subordinates, Nana?

00:15:36.950 --> 00:15:42.080
I'm only here because <i>you</i> said
you couldn't shop on your own.

00:15:42.790 --> 00:15:44.500
You can stop there.

00:15:46.090 --> 00:15:47.090
It's me.

00:15:47.090 --> 00:15:50.130
What're you carrying?

00:15:50.130 --> 00:15:52.430
It looks so familiar.

00:15:52.430 --> 00:15:55.180
Oh, I know! It's Koumi's!

00:15:55.180 --> 00:15:56.970
You think so too, huh?

00:15:56.970 --> 00:15:58.890
All right. I'll be right there.

00:15:59.430 --> 00:16:02.640
Someone tripped the alarm
at the Transportation Museum.

00:16:02.640 --> 00:16:04.440
Trouble?

00:16:04.440 --> 00:16:06.150
Count me in!

00:16:06.150 --> 00:16:10.650
Sakurai, do you understand what "confined to your home" means?

00:16:12.910 --> 00:16:16.330
And on the third floor there's a theater.

00:16:16.330 --> 00:16:19.790
I remember they showed documentaries on various transportation services.

00:16:22.120 --> 00:16:23.710
Here we have the gift shop!

00:16:23.710 --> 00:16:26.920
I always took forever to decide what I wanted.

00:16:30.300 --> 00:16:31.630
But when all's said and done,

00:16:31.630 --> 00:16:36.300
the best part was always the
JNR Class C57 steam locomotive.

00:16:36.300 --> 00:16:38.010
C57 for short!

00:16:38.010 --> 00:16:40.810
It was real popular.
People even nicknamed it "The Lady".

00:16:48.150 --> 00:16:50.360
So we don't get separated.

00:16:50.360 --> 00:16:54.450
Oh, sorry. I guess I got lost on memory lane.

00:16:54.450 --> 00:16:56.620
You've been here before too, right?

00:16:57.990 --> 00:16:59.030
Yeah.

00:17:00.290 --> 00:17:03.790
My life's in danger, and I'm acting like a kid in aвЂ”

00:17:03.790 --> 00:17:04.750
Takayama.

00:17:05.080 --> 00:17:09.630
Do you remember eight years,
three months, and fifteen days ago?

00:17:09.630 --> 00:17:10.210
Huh?

00:17:10.210 --> 00:17:12.590
E-Eight yearsвЂ”

00:17:12.970 --> 00:17:17.470
Eight years, three months, and fifteen days ago.

00:17:19.260 --> 00:17:21.770
U-Um...

00:17:21.770 --> 00:17:23.480
Hey, you two!

00:17:24.350 --> 00:17:25.140
Huh?

00:17:34.240 --> 00:17:38.370
This seems right up Takayama's alley.

00:17:38.370 --> 00:17:41.830
Oh? Never been to the Transportation Museum?

00:17:41.830 --> 00:17:43.580
It's pretty fun, you know.

00:17:49.330 --> 00:17:50.920
DГ©jГ  vu.

00:17:50.920 --> 00:17:54.800
That's another piece of Koumi's uniform, isn't it?

00:17:55.130 --> 00:17:57.760
Maybe they're still close by.

00:17:58.720 --> 00:18:00.140
Get back here!

00:18:06.980 --> 00:18:08.060
Haruka?

00:18:08.060 --> 00:18:09.230
Takayama!

00:18:09.230 --> 00:18:10.520
That's who we're after?

00:18:10.520 --> 00:18:11.400
After them!

00:18:16.700 --> 00:18:18.570
Hurry insideвЂ”

00:18:18.570 --> 00:18:19.740
What?!

00:18:20.660 --> 00:18:22.080
Stop staring!

00:18:23.240 --> 00:18:24.540
Just get inside!

00:18:24.540 --> 00:18:25.410
Takayama?

00:18:25.830 --> 00:18:27.750
Don't come out!

00:18:27.750 --> 00:18:28.750
W-WвЂ”

00:18:30.290 --> 00:18:31.710
Takayama?

00:18:31.710 --> 00:18:33.340
Koumi, you sit tight.

00:18:33.340 --> 00:18:35.210
I'll take care of these clowns!

00:18:35.210 --> 00:18:36.630
No!

00:18:36.630 --> 00:18:38.340
I'm really sorry about today.

00:18:38.340 --> 00:18:41.140
You went through a lot because of me.

00:18:42.350 --> 00:18:44.140
I'm fine with that.

00:18:44.140 --> 00:18:47.930
I'd do anything for yвЂ”

00:18:49.140 --> 00:18:55.570
Plus, if you got hurt or ended up
hating JNR, I'd never forgive myself.

00:18:58.150 --> 00:18:59.530
I have to solve...

00:19:00.860 --> 00:19:03.200
my own problems...

00:19:03.870 --> 00:19:05.240
or there's no point!

00:19:05.830 --> 00:19:07.200
Over here.

00:19:08.250 --> 00:19:09.620
What do you want, bitch?

00:19:21.090 --> 00:19:23.470
Ms. Gonou! Ms. Iida!

00:19:24.050 --> 00:19:24.850
Sakurai!

00:19:25.260 --> 00:19:27.680
You dirty criminal!

00:19:27.680 --> 00:19:28.480
Huh?

00:19:31.140 --> 00:19:31.940
Huh?

00:19:35.650 --> 00:19:38.530
This is just like back then.

00:19:45.530 --> 00:19:47.120
Someone!

00:19:47.120 --> 00:19:48.870
Help!

00:19:49.790 --> 00:19:51.920
Hey, is someone in there?

00:19:52.670 --> 00:19:54.840
Help! Please!

00:19:55.590 --> 00:19:57.460
Just hang in there a little longer.

00:19:57.460 --> 00:19:59.590
I'll call for help, so don't worry.

00:20:00.630 --> 00:20:01.880
Hurry!

00:20:01.880 --> 00:20:03.340
Get me out of here!

00:20:03.340 --> 00:20:06.760
It's so dark and scary in here!

00:20:06.760 --> 00:20:09.640
I'm right here. It's okay.

00:20:09.640 --> 00:20:11.640
Hey, what's your name?

00:20:12.810 --> 00:20:15.440
Haruka Koumi.

00:20:16.520 --> 00:20:17.900
Who are you?

00:20:17.900 --> 00:20:19.190
Me?

00:20:19.190 --> 00:20:20.240
I'm...

00:20:34.330 --> 00:20:35.420
Takayama!

00:20:36.500 --> 00:20:37.420
You...

00:20:38.380 --> 00:20:40.260
You saved me again.

00:20:41.510 --> 00:20:44.380
K-Koumi?

00:20:44.380 --> 00:20:45.590
Seriously.

00:20:46.090 --> 00:20:49.680
What the hell are you doing,
making Haruka strip?!

00:20:49.680 --> 00:20:52.390
Th-That's not what happened, Sakurai!

00:20:52.390 --> 00:20:53.770
Let me explain!

00:20:53.770 --> 00:20:55.730
There were these cat assassins, and...

00:20:57.020 --> 00:20:59.900
Listen to me!

00:21:01.860 --> 00:21:03.950
You were attacked by cat assassins?

00:21:04.490 --> 00:21:06.410
What are you babbling about?

00:21:06.410 --> 00:21:08.620
See, I got this in the mail.

00:21:08.620 --> 00:21:10.580
What? Lemme see.

00:21:12.120 --> 00:21:14.960
"Today could be your last day"?

00:21:16.290 --> 00:21:21.630
"Make sure you're prepared when the time comes".

00:21:21.630 --> 00:21:24.670
"Join JNR Life Insurance today".

00:21:25.470 --> 00:21:26.260
Huh?

00:21:26.970 --> 00:21:28.260
You're kidding.

00:21:28.260 --> 00:21:30.680
<i>This</i> was the threat?

00:21:30.680 --> 00:21:32.850
But then who shot at me?

00:21:33.770 --> 00:21:36.980
Y-You must have been mistaken!

00:21:36.980 --> 00:21:39.520
Talk about the boy who cried wolf.

00:21:39.520 --> 00:21:42.570
You sure had a tough day today, Koumi.

00:21:49.820 --> 00:21:53.330
Please don't hate the rails because of this.

00:21:56.500 --> 00:21:57.920
It's all right.

00:21:57.920 --> 00:22:02.340
My feelings wouldn't change
over something like this.

00:22:02.340 --> 00:22:03.300
Huh?

00:23:40.850 --> 00:23:43.360
When you think JNR's Yokokawa Station,
what comes to mind but their pots-to-go?

00:23:43.360 --> 00:23:45.900
They're one of Japan's premier
popular foods sold at train stations.

00:23:45.900 --> 00:23:47.440
They're to die for!

00:23:47.440 --> 00:23:50.360
Revolutionizing the idea that train station food has to come sold in a box,

00:23:50.360 --> 00:23:53.950
these hot little pots were created for the travelers who wanted a fun,

00:23:53.950 --> 00:23:56.450
home-cooked meal on their journeys!

00:23:56.450 --> 00:23:57.950
They're the bomb!

00:23:57.950 --> 00:24:01.920
Don't hog them all. Share with Takayama, too.

00:24:01.920 --> 00:24:05.090
Rail Wars, Episode Seven: You Look Good in That.

00:24:05.920 --> 00:24:08.960
Be strong, Takayama. I'm cheering for you.
